<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26752" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lippĭtūdo</span></b> ,
			ĭnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>blearedness, rheum</i> or <i>inflammation of the
				eyes</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ab lippitudine usque siccitas ut sit tibi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Rud. 3, 2, 18</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Poen. 1, 2, 182</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">diuturna,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 4, 37, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">molestior,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Att. 8, 12, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sicca,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					28, 11, 47, § 169</span></i>
			; cf. arida, i. q. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξηροφθαλμία</span>, <i><span class="en">Cels. 6, 6, 29</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lippitudines arcere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					28, 4, 7, § 37</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">abstergere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					31, 11, 47, § 125</span></i>
			.</div>
